# Copy this to .env, beside your compose file, and uncomment what you need. No .env at all is fine too.
#
# Most of deadwax is set up in the app instead: open it, then Server settings (the desktop sidebar's
# Settings, or You -> Server settings on a phone) - slskd's address, MusicBrainz's email, Navidrome,
# organizing, cover art, lyrics, the caches. A value saved there applies at once and beats this file.
# This file is for what you'd rather keep out of the app's database, and for what the app can't set.
# Every variable deadwax reads, with its default: docs/configuration.md#environment-variables
#
# One per line as NAME=value, no quotes, and no comment after the value (compose and python-dotenv
# read those differently). Recreate the container after a change: a restart keeps the old values.

# The user and group deadwax runs as, and so the owner of every file it writes - the same pair as
# slskd and your other media containers (`id yourname` on the host prints them). 1000 if unset.
#PUID=1000
#PGID=1000

# slskd: its address as THIS container reaches it, with the scheme, and an API key from slskd's
# configuration. Keep the two together - here, or both in Server settings: an address saved in the app
# takes the key again, typed there, so a key here is used only with the address here.
#SLSKD_URL=http://slskd:5030
#SLSKD_APIKEY=

# Navidrome, which the app's library is: its address as this container reaches it (plus its base path,
# if any), an ordinary account of your own and its password. Together, for the same reason as slskd's.
#NAVIDROME_URL=http://navidrome:4533
#NAVIDROME_USER=
#NAVIDROME_PASSWORD=

# Logins - environment only (Server settings shows them, locked). on: everyone signs in with their
# Navidrome account, and Navidrome's admins are deadwax's. Needs the key below - and BEFORE you turn it
# on, Navidrome set up and Organizing set to copy or move (Server settings -> Library -> Organizing):
# with logins on and organizing still dry run, nothing can be reached, Server settings included.
#AUTH_MODE=on
#
# at least 32 characters: `openssl rand -hex 32`. Here only - a line for it in compose's environment:
# beats this file even when it's empty, and then nobody can sign in.
#DEADWAX_SECRET_KEY=
#
# optional: signs in as `deadwax` with no Navidrome, for when Navidrome is down. The name is public, so
# make it long and random: `openssl rand -base64 18`.
#DEADWAX_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Environment only: behind a reverse proxy that rewrites the Host header, the address you open deadwax
# at, with the scheme (comma-separated for more than one) - or every change is refused as another site's.
#TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://music.example.com
